# p_v6p1 — Weekend Vacuum on the Shelf, Pulled Out for an Evening Clean at 21:00

On weekends the vacuum cleaner rests on storage_shelf_s1 (the upper shelf in the storage room), not on storage_floor_s1 as it does on weekdays. Saturday sightings confirm it on the shelf at both 03:00 and 14:00. It is then pulled down and used on the living room floor at 21:00 (two sightings), and by 23:00 it is back on the storage floor. This is a later, shorter cleaning session than the weekday mid-morning pattern (09:30–11:30 in p_9e4b, or 13:00–15:00 in p_5c8e). The weekend clean happens in the evening, perhaps after the baking and dinner are done and the kitchen is cleared.

The blanket also tells a weekend story: it is on the coffee table at 03:00 (dropped there during the evening before), found at bathroom_shelf_ba1 at 11:00 (likely being washed or folded and stored), and on the bed by 23:00 (tucked in for the night). This differs from the weekday pattern where it oscillates between couch and coffee table.

